Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||12-20-2001||09:55 AM||||My first job out of college as an engineer I worked for a company in pennsylvania who told me they reward employees for their hard work and recognize outstanding achievements.<P> I was the junior engineer on a project with 6 other senior engineers. I personally reduced the cost of the program from $3.5 million dollars to $2.5 million - with some very creative engineering.<P> My boss told me I was the most outstanding engineer he ever met. For my reward I got a 7% raise at the end of a year, instead of the average 4%.<P> No bonus, no percent of the million dollars I had saved the company. I was so PO'd I quit and went to work for Rockwell International instead.||||reg||11
