Z||000017||LZeitgeist||12-20-2001||10:37 AM||||I think they call that the "Goldfish Principle". Supposedly, a goldfish will grow to a larger maximum size if it is kept in a large fishtank, as opposed to staying relatively small if kept in a bowl. <P>In other words, it increases in size according to the size of the container it is kept in. Just like the output vs. income situation... ack. :\||||reg||1
